            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI am afraid, this is an expected behavior of how `:restart` works on Neovim>=0.12.5. It now restores the current session using built-in sessions (see `:h :mksession`), which don't support saving and restoring 'mini.starter' (or other scratch) buffer. To have the same behavior as `:restart` on Neovim<0.12.5, use `:restart!` (with a `!` bang symbol).",
